div.verse:
Let us set before our eyes the holy Apostles; Peter by unjust envy underwent not one or two, but many  
          Labours. sufferings;  
          And so. til at last being martyred, he went to the place of glory that was due unto him.

By envy. For the same cause did Paul in like manner receive the reward of his patience. Seven times  
Having borne seven times bonds, &c. he was in bonds; he was whipped, was stoned; he preached both in the East and in the West;  
He received the, &c. leaving behind him the glorious report of his faith:

And again when he separated himself from Lot, God said unto him;  
          Gen. xiii. 14. Lift up now thine eyes, and look from the place where thou art northward and southward and eastward and  
          Towards the sea. westward for all the land which thou seest, to thee will I give it, and to thy seed for ever.

For so says  
          Holy Word. the Holy Scripture;  
          Isaiah lxvi. 2. upon whom shall I look, even upon him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and that trembles at my word.

Having therefore so many, and such great and glorious 
          Deeds or works. examples, 
          Let us return to the mark of peace given to us from the beginning. let us return to that peace which was the mark that from the beginning was set before us;

For so it is written,  
          Deut. xxxii. 8, 9. When the Most High divided the nations, when he separated the sons of Adam, he set the bounds of the nations, according to the number of his angels;  
          So the LXX. his people Jacob became the portion of the Lord, and Israel the lot of his inheritance.

And in another place he saith,  
          Deut. iv. 34. Behold the Lord taketh unto himself a nation, out of the midst of the nations, as a man taketh the first-fruits of his flower; 
          Num. xxvii. the Most Holy shall come out of that nation.

For having received their command, and being thoroughly assured by the resurrection of our Lord Jesus Christ;  
          1 Thess. i. 5. and convinced by the word of God, with the  
          With the full assurance. fulness of the Holy Spirit, they went abroad, publishing, That the kingdom of God was at hand.
